'' RUN: 'dim as N.T x = N.T( args )' -- a QUALIFIED constructor call as an initialiser -- builds x
'' in place, as the unqualified spelling does: the constructor's @this is x, in a procedure, at
'' module level, and through a nested namespace. It was built in a temporary and its bytes copied
'' out, so an object that hands '@this' away pointed it at a dead slot: FB.AsyncSink's worker,
'' through std/logs, hung the program. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/qualified-ctor-init.bas -o tests/codegen/qualifiedctorinit.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/qualifiedctorinit.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/qualifiedctorinit.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: proc qualified in place: yes v= 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: proc nested in place: yes v= 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: proc unqualified in place: yes v= 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: proc ctors= 3 dtors= 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: module qualified in place: yes v= 4
'' EXPECT-NOT: in place: no
